1.3.0 (2026-10-17)
- The lock menu uses the Pip-Boy's own list style: 14-point rows with the native highlight, like ITEMS, instead of large centred text.
- A details panel beside the list shows the highlighted lock's pin strength, sweet spot and points, using the Pip-Boy's own stat blocks, with your bobby pins, score and best run underneath.
- Selecting the mode row explains Classic and Tumbler.

1.2.1 (2026-10-17)
- Header drawn in the Pip-Boy's own layout (title on the line, info underneath), so nothing is cut off by the rounded corners of the screen.
- Icon is now a Pip-Boy .img, so it shows in ITEMS > MISC.

1.2.0 (2026-10-12)
- Draws Vault Boy picking a lock and a real bobby pin from the Pip-Boy's own game data (Fallout 3 or New Vegas mode) on the menu, the lock screen and the run-over screen. Falls back to the plain look if the data is missing.

1.1.0 (2026-10-09)
- Secret Tumbler mode, unlocked by cleanly picking a Very Hard lock: a realistic pin-tumbler lock with binding order, tension, oversetting and spool pins.

1.0.0 (2026-10-05)
- Initial release of Lockpick, with five lock levels, breakable bobby pins, forcing, and saved progress.
- Use only the SCROLL, TAB and SELECT UI sounds, which every firmware provides.
- Each new bobby pin starts at the top of the lock.
- The outer ring of the lock shakes harder the closer the pin is to breaking.
- The right wheel moves the bobby pin and turning the left wheel either way tries the lock.
- Runs: start with 8 pins, earn pins and score by picking locks, and the run ends when the pins run out. Best score is saved.
- Very Easy locks pay score but no pins.
